# SABOTAGE: T163 / ADR-051 P2 — the reporter sends the tally's WHOLE quantity instead
# of its unreported delta. The provider increments (`samen_stripe`: "action" =>
# "increment"), so every time a reported tally grows, everything already billed is
# billed again: 42 reported, grows to 50, and the provider is sent 50 — 92 billed.
#
# Flips the grown-tally delta test and the growth-during-report test. The fresh-record
# tests stay green (for a never-reported record the delta IS the whole quantity), which
# is why the pre-P2 suite could never have caught a double bill.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/billing_usage_reporter_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a tally that grew after it was reported sends ONLY the delta, under a delta key
# MUST_FAIL: growth DURING a report is marked at the value SENT, and goes out as the next delta
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/billing/usage_reporter.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/billing/usage_reporter.ex
index 2322c18..f73522a 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/billing/usage_reporter.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/billing/usage_reporter.ex
@@ -160,7 +160,8 @@ defmodule Samen.Billing.UsageReporter do
       idempotency_key: idempotency_key(record.id, from, to),
       metric: Map.get(record, :metric),
       # The DELTA: the provider increments, so only the unreported part is sent.
-      quantity: to - from,
+      # SABOTAGE (ADR-051 P2): the whole tally is sent, not the delta.
+      quantity: to,
       timestamp: Map.get(record, :period_end) || Map.get(record, :period_start),
       subscription_id: Map.get(record, :subscription_id),
       provider_ref: Map.get(record, :provider_ref)
